1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Rhea: Tell me about a product project that taught you something.

2
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Dev: I redesigned a support dashboard. Interviews showed that staff lost time switching between tickets and account history.

3
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Rhea: How did you choose what to build?

4
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:14,000
Dev: We prioritized one combined view. We used prototype sessions to test whether staff could find the last contact without opening another page.

5
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:12,000
Dev: I learned that an attractive screen was not enough. We needed realistic ticket histories to reveal missing context.

6
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:12,000
Rhea: What was difficult about working with the team?

7
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:14,000
Dev: We disagreed about how much information belonged on the main screen. Testing helped us compare the alternatives instead of arguing from preference.

8
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:12,000
Dev: I would involve support staff earlier if I repeated the project. Their terminology was different from our internal labels.

9
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:12,000
Rhea: What did you personally contribute?

10
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:12,000
Dev: I led the interviews, made the prototype, and documented the findings. The engineers owned implementation.

11
00:09:54,000 --> 00:10:00,000
Rhea: Thank you. That answers my questions for today.
